import KickoffSession from "../../components/KickoffSession.astro";
---

<KickoffSession
    documentTitle="A decision, not another study. | Canada2080"
    description="Sebastien Gendron on TransPod and how Canada approaches risk, at the Canada2080 kickoff."
    eyebrow="Capacity · 1:55 p.m."
    headline="A decision, not another study."
    name="Sebastien Gendron"
    bio="Sebastien Gendron is co-founder and CEO of TransPod. He works on deep-technology transportation and what it takes to deliver large-scale infrastructure in Canada."
    profileUrl="https://www.transpod.com/about-transpod/"
    profileLabel="TransPod"
    podiumSrc="/images/events/2026-kickoff/gallery/img_5430.jpg"
    podiumAlt="Sebastien Gendron speaking at the podium in a floral shirt."
    photos={[
        {
            src: "/images/events/2026-kickoff/gallery/img_5430.jpg",
            alt: "Sebastien Gendron speaking at the podium in a floral shirt.",
            caption: "At the podium.",
        },
        {
            src: "/images/events/2026-kickoff/gallery/img_5432.jpg",
            alt: "Sebastien Gendron speaking with an orange microphone.",
            caption: "At the microphone.",
        },
    ]}
>
    <p class="lede">
        Useful support would have been timely capital, a real
        reading of the intellectual property, a reason when the answer is no,
        and a decision.
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>
            TransPod is a Canadian deep-tech company about ten
            years old. The proposal is an ultra-high-speed tube between
            Edmonton and Calgary. A vehicle rides in a steel tube on concrete
            pillars, most of the air removed, at more than 300 kilometres an
            hour.
        </li>
        <li>
            He said the Strategic Innovation Fund refused the company twice
            under the previous federal government. Once, because it did not
            understand the intellectual property. Once, in a letter that gave
            no reason.
        </li>
        <li>
            Invest Ontario, he said, would invest only after a further $100
            million private round. His line: they would invest when the company
            no longer needed the money.
        </li>
        <li>
            He quoted an Export Development Canada representative who described
            Canada as a bear coming out of hibernation. The hope, in that line,
            is that the country stays awake.
        </li>
    </ul>
</KickoffSession>
